  "lesson": {
    "title": "El verbo to be (am / is / are)",
    "rule": "El verbo 'to be' cambia según el sujeto: I am (yo soy/estoy), You/We/They are, He/She/It is. Se usa para presentarse, decir origen y describir. Negativo: am not / isn't / aren't. Pregunta: Are you...? / Is he...?",
    "examples": [
      "I am Maria.",
      "You are from Mexico.",
      "She is my friend.",
      "They are students."
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "I is → I am",
      "She are → She is",
      "I am from → NO 'I am from of' (sin 'of')"
    ]
  },
  "pronunciationTip": "En 'Nice to meet you', la 'e' de 'meet' es un sonido largo /iː/ (como 'iiii'). Estírala un poco: mee-eet.",
